  <!--
    The remaining declared cell labels (012-waitlist-card-layout, FR-104). A cell's label IS a resource key: the
    Item declaration in `Database/Seeds/seed_waitlist_request_item_configs/create.sql` declares the label and the
    card resolves it at bind time through `GetLocalized()`. A label with no entry here does NOT draw a blank -
    `GetLocalized()` falls back to the key itself - so the cell read as correct English while never being a
    resolved string, which is how this gap survived. Every one of these is a label the card can draw.

    The three labels this work renames (`Coil Number`, `Home Location`, `Scrap Type`) are deliberately NOT paired
    with their old spellings. The resource index is **case-insensitive** - adding `Coil number` beside
    `Coil Number` fails the build with `PRI277: Conflicting values for resource 'Resources/Coil Number'` - so the
    pre-migration spelling resolves through the canonical key and a second entry would be a duplicate, not a fix.

    These keep the bare-label shape rather than `Feature_Element.Property` because the label IS the key the
    declaration carries; `.github/scripts/validate-csharp-xaml-naming.ps1` lists them as exceptions for that
    reason.
  -->
